    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Nestled within an intimate and highly sought after development of just eight distinguished homes, this magnificent four-bedroom detached residence offers a rare blend of refined luxury, privacy, and coastal charm. Positioned in a quiet cul-de-sac and surrounded by beautifully maintained grounds, the property presents an exceptional opportunity to acquire a truly elegant family home in one of Curracloe’s most desirable residential settings. Extending to an impressive and generously proportioned interior, this superb home has been finished to an exacting standard throughout, with every detail carefully considered to create a sophisticated yet welcoming living environment. From the moment you enter, the sense of quality and craftsmanship is immediately apparent.\r\nThe accommodation is both expansive and beautifully balanced, featuring a series of light-filled reception rooms designed for modern family living and stylish entertaining. A stunning contemporary kitchen forms the heart of the home, complete with premium cabinetry, elegant stone and timber worktops, high-spec integrated appliances, and refined finishes throughout. Large glazing and thoughtfully designed living spaces allow natural light to pour into the home while seamlessly connecting the interior with the surrounding gardens. Upstairs, four luxurious double bedrooms provide exceptional comfort and privacy, including a sumptuous principal suite with bespoke fitted wardrobes and a beautifully appointed en-suite bathroom. The remaining\r\nbedrooms are equally spacious and complemented by a luxurious family bathroom finished in timeless contemporary style. Externally, the property is enveloped by mature, meticulously maintained gardens offering complete tranquillity and privacy. The outdoor space provides a perfect setting for al fresco dining, entertaining, or simply enjoying the peaceful surroundings and wildlife. The mature planting and established boundaries create a secluded sanctuary rarely found in modern developments. Despite its wonderfully peaceful setting, the property enjoys the convenience of being within walking distance of the charming village amenities of Curracloe, while the spectacular coastline and renowned beaches of Curracloe & Raven Forest are just moments away. This enviable location offers an exceptional lifestyle combining coastal beauty with everyday convenience. Properties of this calibre and setting rarely come to the market. Offering luxurious\r\naccommodation, exclusivity, and an unrivalled coastal lifestyle, this outstanding residence is certain to appeal to discerning purchasers seeking an exceptional home in one of Wexford’s most prestigious coastal location. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation Comprises:\r\nEntrance hallway – (4.40m x 3.40m),  Solid timber flooring, feature staircase.\r\nSitting Room – (5.23m x 4.05m), Solid timber flooring, wall panelling.\r\nKitchen/Dining – (4.43 m x 7.95m),  Solid timber flooring, cabinets at waist and eye level, built in \u0003 fridge/ freezer, dishwasher, oven, worktops with solid timber and stone finish, double French doors to rear garden.\r\nUtility – (3.00m x 3.65m),  Tile flooring, cabinets at waist and eye level, plumbed for washing machine, access to rear.\r\nGuest WC – (1.10m x 1.80m),  Tile flooring, WC, WHB.\r\nLiving Room – (4.50m x 4.05m), Solid timber flooring, feature stove, built in storage.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\n\r\nLanding – (5.43m x 3.40m), Carpet flooring, seating area with elevated views to the front, attic hatch.\r\nBedroom No. 1 – (3.15m x 4.05m),  Carpet flooring.\r\nBedroom No.2 – (3.86m x 4.05m), Carpet flooring, large wardrobe space.\r\nBedroom No. 3 – (4.26m x 4.05m),  Carpet flooring, large wardrobe space.\r\nBathroom – (3.45m x 2.25m),  Tile flooring, WC, WHB, bathtub, enclosed shower, tiled walls\r\nMaster Bedroom – (3.45m x 3.90m),  Carpet flooring, wall panelling, large wardrobe space.\r\nEn-Suite – (1.53m x 2.33m), Fully tiled, WC, WHB, enclosed shower.\r\n\r\nOutside: Mature and established gardens to the rear with a range of trees, plants & shrubbery, side entrance, green- house, poly tunnel, pond, chicken coop, parking to front.\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, private sewerage, oil fired central heating.\r\nBER: B3 Ber No: 106970536 Performance indicator: 145.76 kWh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072"
      },
